==English==
[[File:Basel 2012-10-05 Batch 2 (25).JPG|thumb|A thyroid gland prepared in 1925 as a [[medical]] [[specimen]] in the collection of the Anatomisches Museum, [[Basel]], [[Switzerland]]]]

===Etymology===
From {{cal|en|la-new|glandula thyreoidea|notext=1}}, coined by [[w:Thomas_Wharton (anatomist)|Thomas Wharton]] in 1656.

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{lb|en|anatomy}} A large [[butterfly]]-[[shaped]] [[endocrine gland]] situated on the front of the [[neck]] that produces various [[hormone]]s.

====Related terms====
* {{l|en|hyperthyroidism}}
* {{l|en|hypothyroidism}}
* {{l|en|thyroidectomy}}

